A||||5||William Federle||Strut tower insulation||||1||
Z||000000||William Federle||06-20-2000||06:52 AM||||I want to install a junction block or terminal strip on the strut tower near the battery. However there's insulation that's about 1/2 to 3/4 inch thick in that area. Does anyone know if this is absolutely necessary? I can't think of a reason for that area to be insulated.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||dman||06-20-2000||02:50 PM||||I believe you can safely remove that insulation. It helps with sound/vibration but I think its more trouble than it is worth --- tends to collect dirt and grime. In fact, if you remove it completely you will end up exposing an opening by the battery that helps provide just a little bit more airflow to help cool your engine compartment and battery. It seems to be a fiberglass cloth so I'd recommend wearing long sleeves and gloves to avoid getting any on you (a dust mask helps too). Some people are sensitive to this type of material (makes them itch).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||06-20-2000||04:41 PM||||I removed the insulation from both sides of my engine compartment years ago and I can't tell any difference in noise.  It makes it much easier to keep the area clean.  I wouldn't recommend pulling off the piece on the firewall, though.  I tried and ended up putting it back on so I could hear the radio. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000003||William Federle||06-20-2000||07:48 PM||||Thanks for the replies. I always feel better about doing something to this car if I can get a little advice first.<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 06-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||jlruiz67||06-21-2000||04:22 PM||||Hello<BR>I thank you for your post on removing the insulation material. I read your post and started removing it from my Fiero and what do you know. Everything under the material was finger tight and some supports where completle loose, also found a big leak somewhere in there that I have to clean and find out where the hell it is comming from. Well if it turns out to be brake fluid you could have saved my life with something so simple as removing the insulation material. Thank you for your post and keep them coming. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||William Federle||06-21-2000||08:18 PM||||I'm glad to hear that you found the leak. It's just one more reason to appreciate this forum. With so many people posting and answering, its a good place to find good insights.||||reg||1
